     "text": "```python\ndef product_array_except_self(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the product of all elements in the array except the current element.\n    \n    This function computes the product array where each element at index i is the product\n    of all elements in the input array except the element at index i. The solution uses\n    two passes to efficiently compute the result in O(n) time and O(1) space, excluding\n    the output array.\n    \n    Args:\n        nums (List[int]): A list of integers.\n        \n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A list where each element at index i is the product of all elements\n                   in nums except the element at index i.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(nums)\n    result = [1] * n\n    \n    # First pass: multiply all elements to the left of each index\n    left = 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        result[i] *= left\n        left *= nums[i]\n    \n    # Second pass: multiply all elements to the right of each index\n    right = 1\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        result[i] *= right\n        right *= nums[i]\n    \n    return result\n```",
